The projection from the inverse limit onto stage n, as a bare function `projInfFun`, reads the n-th coordinate of a compatible sequence. `projInfFun.preservesDirectedSup` says that function preserves directed suprema: the chosen coordinate of the supremum of a nonempty directed set of compatible sequences equals the supremum of that coordinate on the set. `projInf` is the same function as a Scott-continuous map, with continuity coming from that preservation.
